l Revenue Code” means the Internal Revenue Code of 1986, as amended.","section":"","block":853,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-097350","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001839530","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1839530/000110465926097350/xbp-20260630xex10d3.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a4cc3e24933b92bfac040b3aeb97fc8f87a28efd531fe6aaf2c5bd4dfd1a6979.bin","sha256":"a4cc3e24933b92bfac040b3aeb97fc8f87a28efd531fe6aaf2c5bd4dfd1a6979"}},{"id":"256b87cef882742ae83ae6623ecf9a40d936a40ebb0177e4461993546e73b179","quote":"(7)Investments received in connection with the bankruptcy or reorganization of, or settlement of delinquent accounts and disputes with or judgments against, customers and suppliers, in each case in the ordinary course of business of the Borrowers, any Subsidiary or Investments acquired by the Borrowers or any of its Subsidiaries as a result of a foreclosure by the Borrowers or any of its Subsidiaries, respectively, with respect to any secured Investments or other transfer of title with respect to any secured Investment in default;","context":"(6)advances of payroll payments, business related travel expenses, moving expenses and other similar expenses and expenses to employees in the ordinary course of business;","section":"business, operations, assets, or financial condition of the Lead Borrower and its Subsidiaries, taken as a whole.","block":931,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-097350","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001839530","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1839530/000110465926097350/xbp-20260630xex10d3.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a4cc3e24933b92bfac040b3aeb97fc8f87a28efd531fe6aaf2c5bd4dfd1a6979.bin","sha256":"a4cc3e24933b92bfac040b3aeb97f